  "answer": "No. The Aussie dollar is strong against the yen right now, even though it has slipped a little in recent weeks.\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 bought ¥109.67 on 16 October 2026 (RBA 4pm rate).\n- **Over the past 21 months:** It was ¥91.43 in April 2025 and ¥96.14 in January 2025. That means the Aussie is up about 14% on January 2025 and about 20% on April 2025.\n- **Peak:** It reached about ¥114.3 in April 2026 and ¥114.5 in August 2026. Those are the highest month-end levels in the data since 2025.\n- **Recent dip:** It fell from ¥114.63 on 1 September to about ¥110 by mid-September. It has stayed around ¥110 through October, a drop of about 4% from early September.\n\nThe recent dip looks like Aussie weakness more than yen strength. AUD/USD fell from 0.717 to 0.695 over the same period.\n\nThe data I have only starts in 2023, so I can't compare the current level with longer-run history. The Aussie is well above where it was in 2025.",
